      ],
      "id": "xu6t91m"
    },
    {
      "id": "ay6919z",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Radius and General Facts about the Earth"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Earth's interior consists of three main concentric layers: the Crust, Mantle, and Core.",
        "The Crust is categorized into Continental Crust (rich in Silica and Aluminium - SIAL) and Oceanic Crust (rich in Silica and Magnesium - SIMA).",
        "The Mantle extends up to 2,900 km deep, containing the ductile Asthenosphere which is the primary source of volcanic magma.",
        "The Core is composed mainly of Nickel and Iron (NIFE) and is divided into a liquid Outer Core and a solid Inner Core.",
        "Seismic wave behavior reveals internal discontinuities: Conrad, Mohorovičić (Moho), Repetti, Gutenberg, and Lehmann."
      ],
      "id": "3efe2bp"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ffs17fw",
      "content": "• Average radius of Earth: about 6371 km."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "r0ha2rc",
      "content": "• Earth's interior temperature increases with depth (geothermal gradient)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ffs3clm",
      "content": "• Density also increases toward the center."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "591gtzg",
      "content": "• The Earth is composed mainly of iron, oxygen, silicon, magnesium and nickel."
    },
    {
      "id": "3c4jnzk",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. Sources of Information about the Earth's Interior"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "q0fqxaw",
      "content": "A. Direct Sources"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "02mo6j0",
      "content": "• Mining and deep drilling projects."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "t19plc3",
      "content": "• Volcanic eruptions bring materials from inside the Earth."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "30vgbck",
      "content": "B. Indirect Sources"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "557rxnt",
      "content": "• Seismic waves produced by earthquakes."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "iznc1t4",
      "content": "• Gravitational force studies."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ic18f0y",
      "content": "• Magnetic field observations."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3lk5eja",
      "content": "• Meteorite composition which is similar to Earth's interior."
    },
    {
      "id": "zjwud4q",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "3. Major Layers of the Earth"
    },
